From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:39:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bonito: disable display multirect to stop the compositor
 wedging

The display dies intermittently: the panel goes black, the framework
still reports the display Awake and ON, and nothing short of a reboot
brings it back. Waking, power cycling and unblanking the backlight by
hand all fail, and a screencap of the wedged device is uniformly black,
so the compositor has stopped producing frames rather than the panel
having lost power.

The kernel names the cause:

  [drm:sde_crtc_atomic_check] r1 only virt plane:89 not supported

sde_crtc_atomic_check() pairs the planes staged on each SSPP, then
rejects any SSPP left holding a single plane when that plane is the
virtual one. So the pipe allocator asked for the second rect of a pipe
without the first. drmModeAtomicCommit returns EINVAL, SDM reports
'Composition strategies exhausted', and SurfaceFlinger can present
nothing.

The failing planes are 86, 89 and 91, which debugfs shows are the
virtual twins of the three DMA pipes (src_blk 0x25000/0x27000/0x29000,
xin 1/5/9). The allocator is PipeAlloc in libsdmextension.so, a prebuilt,
so the assignment cannot be fixed here -- but the same blob reads
vendor.display.disable_multirect, which turns the mechanism off.

Verified on hardware: with the property set and the composer restarted,
ten sleep/wake cycles produced no new errors at all, where before it
failed on nearly every wake.

Costs the five secondary rects, leaving one composition layer per SSPP
and GPU fallback for heavy stacks.
---
 device.mk | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/device.mk b/device.mk
index ea2f9aad..5fb98c61 100644
--- a/device.mk
+++ b/device.mk
@@ -265,6 +265,16 @@ PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += \
 PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += \
     vendor.display.disable_inline_rotator=1
 
+# The pipe allocator in libsdmextension.so (prebuilt) sometimes stages the
+# second rect of a DMA pipe without the first. sde_crtc_atomic_check() rejects
+# an SSPP left holding only its virtual plane, so drmModeAtomicCommit fails
+# EINVAL, SDM exhausts every composition strategy and SurfaceFlinger stops
+# presenting -- a black panel the framework still believes is on, recoverable
+# only by rebooting. Disabling multirect costs the five secondary rects and
+# keeps one composition layer per SSPP.
+PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += \
+    vendor.display.disable_multirect=1
+
 # Enable camera EIS3.0
 PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += \
     persist.camera.is_type=5 \
